paragraphs:
from self-trust,
from hidden sin,
from the illusion of control—

“But He was pierced for our transgressions;
He was crushed for our iniquities;
the punishment that brought us peace was on Him…”

“Who, being in very nature God, did not consider equality with God something to be used to his own advantage;
rather, he made himself nothing…
he humbled himself by becoming obedient to death—even death on a cross.”

“Behold, this has touched your lips;
your guilt is taken away,
and your sin atoned for.” (Isaiah 6:7)

If you’ve been fighting uncovered,
if you’ve been losing silent battles,
if shame has been louder than grace—

“The Lord has heard the sound of my weeping.
The Lord has heard my plea;
the Lord accepts my prayer.” (Psalm 6:8–9)

“But He was pierced for our transgressions;
He was crushed for our iniquities…
and by His wounds we are healed.” — Isaiah 53:5

“He was oppressed and afflicted, yet He did not open His mouth;
He was led like a lamb to the slaughter.”
— Isaiah 53:7

And Manoah knew—
if God was entrusting them with purpose,
their lifestyle had to align with it.

“I am the vine; you are the branches.
If you remain in Me and I in you, you will bear much fruit;
apart from Me you can do nothing.”
